WEBVTT

00:00:05.977 --> 00:00:12.142
Black Cat Presents I Want to Be You by Andrea M.

00:00:12.202 --> 00:00:37.388
Hutchinson Copyright Black Cat Publishing Chapter 1 Teammates Hurry up girls, the match starts in 10 minutes.

00:00:37.448 --> 00:00:40.389
Says Miss Stevens the PE teacher.

00:00:40.449 --> 00:00:44.020
And remember, what are we going to do?

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.610
Win!

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.451
Everyone shouts.

00:00:47.511 --> 00:00:52.672
Miss Stevens leaves the changing rooms and Rosie starts putting on makeup.

00:00:52.732 --> 00:00:55.253
Don't look at me like that, Holly.

00:00:55.313 --> 00:00:56.574
Says Rosie.

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:58.313
You know it!

00:00:58.373 --> 00:01:03.184
I start to say, against school rules to wear makeup.

00:01:03.244 --> 00:01:07.236
She says in a silly voice and everyone laughs.

00:01:07.296 --> 00:01:09.818
You're so boring, Holly.

00:01:09.878 --> 00:01:12.469
Says Jane, Rosie's best friend.

00:01:12.529 --> 00:01:15.481
There's a photographer from the local newspaper.

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.342
I need to look my best.

00:01:17.402 --> 00:01:18.762
Says Rosie.

00:01:18.822 --> 00:01:23.813
Rosie is the team captain, our best player and my cousin.

00:01:23.873 --> 00:01:29.136
We were even born on the same day, but we aren't similar at all.

00:01:29.196 --> 00:01:31.318
Rosie likes sport.

00:01:31.378 --> 00:01:33.169
I like painting.

00:01:33.229 --> 00:01:36.553
I love chocolate and baking cakes.

00:01:36.612 --> 00:01:39.364
Rosie is always on a diet.

00:01:39.424 --> 00:01:48.522
This week, she's only eating things that begin with the letter P, pineapple, peppers and peas.

00:01:48.582 --> 00:01:55.854
I like pineapples, but every day, for seven days, she's crazy.

00:01:55.914 --> 00:01:59.656
Her family is rich, mine is not.

00:01:59.716 --> 00:02:08.189
We're not poor, but Rosie's mum and dad, aren't Lily and Uncle Pete, have lots and lots of money.

00:02:08.249 --> 00:02:11.151
They go on holiday in the Seychelles.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:14.712
We go on holiday in a caravan in Scotland.

00:02:14.772 --> 00:02:22.775
They moved house last month, Aunt Lily told mum it was because they needed an extra room for their gym and sauna.

00:02:22.835 --> 00:02:25.756
We don't really see them very often.

00:02:25.816 --> 00:02:30.016
To be honest, we really couldn't be more different if we tried.

00:02:30.076 --> 00:02:34.987
The only thing Rosie and I both have is blonde hair.

00:02:35.047 --> 00:02:40.008
Rosie's is long and straight and it always looks perfect.

00:02:40.068 --> 00:02:47.496
Mine is short and curly and I always look like a clown Ready!

00:02:47.556 --> 00:02:50.398
Rosie asked the team with a nervous smile.

00:02:50.458 --> 00:02:51.538
Yes!

00:02:51.598 --> 00:02:53.260
But let's go!

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.942
The team follows head to the gym.

00:02:56.002 --> 00:03:00.454
As usual, I'm the last one to leave the changing rooms.

00:03:00.514 --> 00:03:04.888
I sit down with the other reserves and cross my fingers.

00:03:04.948 --> 00:03:06.779
Please!

00:03:06.839 --> 00:03:09.702
I hope they don't need me.

00:03:09.762 --> 00:03:12.224
I hate basketball.

00:03:12.284 --> 00:03:20.138
I hate science, Sudoku and supermodels, but I hate basketball most.

00:03:20.198 --> 00:03:22.608
The game starts well.

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:25.780
Rosie scores twice in five minutes.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.411
Every time she scores, she smiles at the photographer.

00:03:30.471 --> 00:03:34.492
Across the gym, Ben is sitting with his friends.

00:03:34.552 --> 00:03:39.288
I think Ben is gorgeous, but he doesn't know I exist.

00:03:39.348 --> 00:03:43.523
No boy like Ben ever looks at a girl like me.

00:03:43.583 --> 00:03:46.204
I look at the clock.

00:03:46.264 --> 00:03:51.645
210, 209, 08, 07.

00:03:51.705 --> 00:03:53.026
Great!

00:03:53.086 --> 00:03:56.596
Only two more minutes before the game is over.

00:03:56.656 --> 00:03:58.697
The score is 22-23.

00:03:58.757 --> 00:04:03.108
The other team is winning but Rosie has the ball.

00:04:03.168 --> 00:04:06.583
She runs past one player and then another.

00:04:06.643 --> 00:04:12.281
As she gets closer to the basket, everyone stands up and shouts, Rosie!

00:04:12.341 --> 00:04:13.312
Rosie!

00:04:13.372 --> 00:04:14.894
Rosie!

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:24.922
Just as I start to relax and think that I won't have to play, a player from the other team runs into Rosie and she falls to the floor.

00:04:24.982 --> 00:04:26.303
Rosie!

00:04:26.363 --> 00:04:27.754
Are you okay?

00:04:27.814 --> 00:04:29.276
I run to her.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.966
My foot!

00:04:31.026 --> 00:04:33.479
It hurts!

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.904
Is she going to be okay?

00:04:35.964 --> 00:04:37.830
I asked Miss Stevens.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:40.012
But she doesn't answer.

00:04:40.072 --> 00:04:42.586
She looks very worried.

00:04:42.646 --> 00:04:47.162
It's okay, Rosie, I say, helping her to stand up.

00:04:47.222 --> 00:04:49.208
I look after you.

00:04:49.268 --> 00:04:50.941
Holly!

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.791
Miss Stevens' shouts.

00:04:52.851 --> 00:04:54.542
Where are you going?

00:04:54.602 --> 00:04:57.443
With my cousin to the nurse, of course.

00:04:57.503 --> 00:04:58.864
You're a reserve.

00:04:58.924 --> 00:05:00.304
The team needs you.

00:05:00.364 --> 00:05:01.965
Get on the court.

00:05:02.025 --> 00:05:02.926
But...

00:05:02.986 --> 00:05:05.366
Can't you choose someone else?

00:05:05.426 --> 00:05:06.767
No!

00:05:06.827 --> 00:05:08.468
It's okay.

00:05:08.528 --> 00:05:09.838
Says Rosie.

00:05:09.898 --> 00:05:10.889
Go on.

00:05:10.949 --> 00:05:13.300
We've got to win this match, Holly.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.980
I'll be okay.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.755
I don't want to, but I walk back onto the court.

00:05:18.815 --> 00:05:21.269
The referee gives me the ball.

00:05:21.329 --> 00:05:23.440
Why are you giving me the ball?

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:24.431
I ask.

00:05:24.491 --> 00:05:26.292
Wake up, Holly!

00:05:26.352 --> 00:05:27.972
Shouts, Miss Stevens.

00:05:28.032 --> 00:05:31.154
You've got to take the penalty, but...

00:05:31.214 --> 00:05:33.185
Come on, Holly!

00:05:33.245 --> 00:05:35.226
You can do it!

00:05:35.286 --> 00:05:37.028
Shouts the team.

00:05:37.088 --> 00:05:40.039
The basket's only four metres away.

00:05:40.099 --> 00:05:42.891
It can't be difficult, can it?

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:44.551
I aim.

00:05:44.611 --> 00:05:46.342
Close my eyes.

00:05:46.402 --> 00:05:48.165
Open them again.

00:05:48.224 --> 00:05:52.107
Take a deep breath, and shoot.

00:05:52.167 --> 00:06:00.960
Everyone watches in silence as the ball bounces first on the backboard, then on the ring, and then...

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:03.941
NO!

00:06:04.001 --> 00:06:11.024
Everyone says at the same time, the ball misses the basket and falls to the ground.

00:06:11.083 --> 00:06:15.580
The final whistle goes, game over.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:21.730
The other team jump up, they lift the winners trophy and the supporters cheer.

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:25.914
They look so happy when they smile for the newspaper photo.

00:06:25.974 --> 00:06:33.470
Sorry Jane, Susan, I say to my teammates, but they turn away.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.742
Even Miss Stevens looks angry with me.

00:06:36.802 --> 00:06:44.582
The team walk back to the changing rooms in silence and I am left alone.

00:06:44.642 --> 00:06:56.593
Chapter 2 I Hate My Life This school is very quiet when I'm ready to leave.

00:06:56.652 --> 00:07:00.106
I'm glad because I don't want to see anybody.

00:07:00.166 --> 00:07:05.200
But before I go home, I need to know that Rosie is okay.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:10.954
When I get to the nurse's office, Jane and Julie are standing in front of the door.

00:07:11.013 --> 00:07:14.696
When they see me, they stop talking.

00:07:14.756 --> 00:07:16.686
What do you want?"

00:07:16.746 --> 00:07:18.048
asks Jane.

00:07:18.107 --> 00:07:21.050
She doesn't smile.

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:23.162
I want to see Rosie.

00:07:23.222 --> 00:07:26.006
I want to see if she's okay, I say.

00:07:26.066 --> 00:07:30.400
Well, she doesn't want to see you, says Julie.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:34.234
Please, I say, moving towards the door.

00:07:34.294 --> 00:07:38.746
But they stand closer together, stopping me from going in.

00:07:38.806 --> 00:07:42.247
Don't you understand, says Jane.

00:07:42.307 --> 00:07:47.871
She doesn't want to see you.

00:07:47.891 --> 00:07:52.744
I open my mouth to say something horrible to them.

00:07:52.804 --> 00:07:59.540
But if I try to speak, I will cry, and I will not cry in front of those two.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:01.551
So I walk away.

00:08:01.611 --> 00:08:07.052
When I turn the corner, I start to cry, and then I start to run.

00:08:07.112 --> 00:08:09.460
I hate this school.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.312
I never want to come back.

00:08:12.372 --> 00:08:13.622
Never!

00:08:13.682 --> 00:08:20.367
I run away from the school, and when I turn a corner, I run straight into Sarah.

00:08:20.427 --> 00:08:25.701
She's coming out of the library with some books, and they all fall to the ground.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:29.622
Sorry, I say, as I help her pick up the books.

00:08:29.682 --> 00:08:32.105
Advanced German grammar.

00:08:32.164 --> 00:08:34.236
Genetics today.

00:08:34.295 --> 00:08:36.840
Sarah is my best friend.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:42.994
The only problem is, her idea of fun is extra chemistry homework.

00:08:43.054 --> 00:08:45.846
I heard about the basketball match.

00:08:45.906 --> 00:08:49.476
I'm sorry you didn't win, but it wasn't your fault.

00:08:49.536 --> 00:08:51.567
I tried to smile.

00:08:51.627 --> 00:08:54.932
I know she's only trying to make me feel better.

00:08:54.992 --> 00:08:57.197
But then she continues.

00:08:57.257 --> 00:09:02.390
I mean, Miss Stevens knows you're not very good at taking penalties.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:11.314
She sees the look on my face and quickly says, but you were good at other things, like French.

00:09:11.374 --> 00:09:15.496
No really, you did really well in the last test.

00:09:15.556 --> 00:09:18.708
Sarah, I got a C.

00:09:18.768 --> 00:09:21.470
Well, that's good for you.

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:25.114
After a pause, she tries again.

00:09:25.174 --> 00:09:28.006
That's it, she says.

00:09:28.066 --> 00:09:32.329
Just as Einstein probably did when he made his discoveries.

00:09:32.388 --> 00:09:33.940
The baking.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.602
Your chocolate cake is the best in the world.

00:09:37.661 --> 00:09:41.342
We walked the rest of the way home in silence.

00:09:41.402 --> 00:09:45.122
I'm going to the fair with my parents tomorrow night.

00:09:45.182 --> 00:09:47.464
She says when we get to my house.

00:09:47.524 --> 00:09:49.715
Do you want to come with us?

00:09:49.775 --> 00:09:52.858
Maybe it will make you feel better.

00:09:52.918 --> 00:09:58.901
Sarah is the only teenager on the planet who will be going to the fair with her mum and dad.

00:09:58.961 --> 00:10:01.292
But I have nothing better to do.

00:10:01.352 --> 00:10:03.824
Excellent, she says.

00:10:03.884 --> 00:10:07.357
And with a big smile, she walks away.

00:10:07.417 --> 00:10:11.979
Later that evening, Mum and I sit down to have dinner.

00:10:12.039 --> 00:10:15.370
Some people don't eat anything when they're sad.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:19.301
Some people are never sad because their lives are perfect.

00:10:19.361 --> 00:10:22.272
People like Rosie, for example.

00:10:22.332 --> 00:10:26.423
That's why they can live on half a carat a day.

00:10:26.483 --> 00:10:32.468
But other people, like me, when things go wrong, they bake.

00:10:32.528 --> 00:10:36.383
And when they are finished baking, they bake some more.

00:10:36.443 --> 00:10:39.794
And then they sit down and eat the lot.

00:10:39.854 --> 00:10:50.278
When Tad comes home, he sits down at the table with the big smile, ready to hear my news and asks, How's my little champion?

00:10:50.338 --> 00:10:57.059
Mum puts his plate in front of him and says, I always thought basketball was a silly game.

00:10:57.119 --> 00:10:58.700
Never mind, Holly.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:02.912
It's your birthday on Sunday, and Monday is a bank holiday.

00:11:02.972 --> 00:11:06.375
Dad knows then that things didn't go well.

00:11:06.435 --> 00:11:08.426
He stops smiling.

00:11:08.486 --> 00:11:12.178
Oh, well, I'm sure you did your best.

00:11:12.238 --> 00:11:15.881
He says, I only played for 30 seconds.

00:11:15.941 --> 00:11:18.803
Well, it can't be your fault then, can it?

00:11:18.863 --> 00:11:20.124
He smiles again.

00:11:20.144 --> 00:11:23.505
I missed a penalty.

00:11:23.565 --> 00:11:25.795
No smile.

00:11:25.855 --> 00:11:36.268
In the last minute of the game, after a long silence, he says, But your chocolate cake is the best in the world.

00:11:36.328 --> 00:11:40.338
He smiles once more and reaches for the salt.

00:11:40.398 --> 00:11:44.789
Later, I sit in bed eating chocolate ice cream.

00:11:44.849 --> 00:11:49.780
Why can't anyone understand that I don't want to be known because I make nice cakes?

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:53.268
I want to be funny, pretty, clever.

00:11:53.328 --> 00:11:58.049
No one will ever want to go to the fair or anywhere else with me now.

00:11:58.069 --> 00:12:01.902
No one except Sarah and her mum and dad.

00:12:01.962 --> 00:12:05.415
Why is life so wrong?

00:12:05.435 --> 00:12:05.896
Why?

00:12:05.956 --> 00:12:06.937
Why?

00:12:06.957 --> 00:12:11.701
I don't hear the phone ringing.

00:12:11.721 --> 00:12:13.852
Holly, there's a call for you.

00:12:13.912 --> 00:12:15.374
Shouts mum.

00:12:15.434 --> 00:12:17.706
Say that I'm sleeping.

00:12:17.766 --> 00:12:19.483
I shout back.

00:12:19.543 --> 00:12:22.189
It's a boy called Ben.

00:12:22.249 --> 00:12:24.610
He says he goes to your school.

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:26.400
Are you sure?

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:31.811
Before she can continue, I'm out of bed and running down the stairs.

00:12:31.871 --> 00:12:32.782
Hello?

00:12:32.802 --> 00:12:34.992
Hello, Holly.

00:12:35.052 --> 00:12:37.903
I just wanted to know how you're feeling.

00:12:37.963 --> 00:12:43.414
You looked really disappointed after the match, but it wasn't your fault.

00:12:43.474 --> 00:12:45.454
Er, I...

00:12:45.514 --> 00:12:48.205
Do you want to go to the fair tomorrow night?

00:12:48.265 --> 00:12:49.755
He says quickly.

00:12:49.815 --> 00:12:52.145
It seems like he's nervous.

00:12:52.205 --> 00:12:53.436
I...

00:12:53.496 --> 00:12:57.626
A group of us are going and I thought, well, I'd...

00:12:57.686 --> 00:13:00.217
I'd really like you to come too.

00:13:00.277 --> 00:13:02.637
Holly, are you still there?

00:13:02.697 --> 00:13:03.698
Yes.

00:13:03.758 --> 00:13:06.728
Oh, why can't I be like Rosie?

00:13:06.788 --> 00:13:10.309
She's never nervous when she speaks to boys.

00:13:10.369 --> 00:13:13.319
I mean, what time?

00:13:13.379 --> 00:13:15.410
We can meet there at six.

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:16.740
Is that okay?

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:18.048
Okay.

00:13:18.108 --> 00:13:21.016
I'm going out with Ben.

00:13:21.076 --> 00:13:23.887
I'm going out with Ben.

00:13:23.947 --> 00:13:25.057
Bye.

00:13:25.117 --> 00:13:26.178
Bye.

00:13:26.238 --> 00:13:27.838
Oh, and Holly.

00:13:27.898 --> 00:13:28.788
Yes?

00:13:28.848 --> 00:13:31.439
I'm really glad you said yes.

00:13:31.499 --> 00:13:33.450
And then he hangs up.

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:38.051
And like an idiot, I stand there, holding onto the phone.

00:13:38.111 --> 00:13:40.922
My heart beating strong and loud.

00:13:40.982 --> 00:13:43.333
My legs feeling weak as jelly.

00:13:43.393 --> 00:13:47.267
But wanting to dance around the room all at the same time.

00:13:47.327 --> 00:13:52.314
I don't have bad memories of the match now.

00:13:52.374 --> 00:13:58.828
Listening activity.

00:13:58.888 --> 00:14:02.692
Hello.

00:14:02.712 --> 00:14:03.842
Hello.

00:14:03.902 --> 00:14:05.634
Can I speak to Amy, please?

00:14:05.694 --> 00:14:06.414
Speaking.

00:14:06.434 --> 00:14:07.816
Hi, Amy.

00:14:07.876 --> 00:14:08.676
It's Mark.

00:14:08.736 --> 00:14:09.607
Hi, Mark.

00:14:09.667 --> 00:14:10.627
How are you?

00:14:10.688 --> 00:14:12.239
I'm fine, thanks.

00:14:12.299 --> 00:14:14.791
I was going to phone you after tea.

00:14:14.851 --> 00:14:17.554
Are you going to Lucy's birthday party?

00:14:17.614 --> 00:14:21.268
I wanted to, but my dad has got to go to work.

00:14:21.328 --> 00:14:22.899
He can't take me.

00:14:22.959 --> 00:14:25.231
We can pick you up if you want.

00:14:25.291 --> 00:14:26.322
Really?

00:14:26.382 --> 00:14:28.124
That would be great.

00:14:28.184 --> 00:14:29.084
Sure.

00:14:29.144 --> 00:14:32.397
I'll check with Dad, but I'm sure it will be okay.

00:14:32.457 --> 00:14:33.658
What time?

00:14:33.718 --> 00:14:35.980
The party starts at six.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.372
What about quarter two then?

00:14:38.432 --> 00:14:40.373
We don't want to get there first.

00:14:40.434 --> 00:14:41.404
Okay.

00:14:41.464 --> 00:14:42.906
Quarter to six.

00:14:42.966 --> 00:14:43.866
See you then.

00:14:43.886 --> 00:14:44.156
Bye.

00:14:44.216 --> 00:14:47.414
Bye.

00:14:47.474 --> 00:14:53.325
Chapter 3 Friends again?

00:14:53.345 --> 00:15:03.746
The next morning, a knock on my bedroom door wakes me up, just when I was having a wonderful dream about Ben.

00:15:03.806 --> 00:15:10.098
I want to go back to sleep, back to my dream, but then Rosie is in my room.

00:15:10.158 --> 00:15:12.614
I wanted to come and see you.

00:15:12.674 --> 00:15:14.906
Aunt Violet said it was okay.

00:15:14.966 --> 00:15:17.258
You don't mind, do you?

00:15:17.318 --> 00:15:19.731
She looks like she's sorry.

00:15:19.791 --> 00:15:22.504
She looks like she wants to be friends.

00:15:22.564 --> 00:15:25.216
She doesn't look like Rosie at all.

00:15:25.276 --> 00:15:26.667
How's your foot?

00:15:26.727 --> 00:15:27.938
I ask.

00:15:27.998 --> 00:15:31.622
I tried to hide last night's empty ice cream box.

00:15:31.682 --> 00:15:35.056
I see the spoon just before Rosie sits on it.

00:15:35.116 --> 00:15:37.470
I tried to come and see you.

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:39.152
But Jane and Julie...

00:15:39.212 --> 00:15:40.274
I know.

00:15:40.334 --> 00:15:42.326
That's why I'm here.

00:15:42.386 --> 00:15:44.258
She holds my hand.

00:15:44.318 --> 00:15:47.042
I was horrible to you yesterday.

00:15:47.102 --> 00:15:48.624
We all were.

00:15:48.684 --> 00:15:50.356
That's okay.

00:15:50.416 --> 00:15:52.218
Let's forget about it.

00:15:52.278 --> 00:15:53.470
Really?

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:54.870
I smile.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:56.364
Really?

00:15:56.424 --> 00:16:01.308
Can I do anything to show you how sorry I am, anything at all?

00:16:01.368 --> 00:16:03.628
Do you want to come and see the new house?

00:16:03.688 --> 00:16:06.200
You can use our gym and sauna.

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:10.521
I want to say yes, but then I see myself in the mirror.

00:16:10.581 --> 00:16:14.622
The last thing I want is Rosie to see me in a swimming costume.

00:16:14.682 --> 00:16:19.364
I look at Rosie sitting next to me, perfect as usual.

00:16:19.424 --> 00:16:23.216
I think for a moment and then I have an idea.

00:16:23.276 --> 00:16:26.732
Actually, there is something.

00:16:26.792 --> 00:16:31.278
Two hours later, we're in one of Rosie's favorite shops.

00:16:31.338 --> 00:16:33.428
But I can't buy it.

00:16:33.488 --> 00:16:35.099
It's very short.

00:16:35.159 --> 00:16:37.229
My dad'll grant me.

00:16:37.289 --> 00:16:40.070
Trust me, says Rosie.

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:42.250
It's the latest fashion.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:49.712
You can't go out with the most gorgeous boy in school wearing something that your dad likes.

00:16:49.772 --> 00:16:53.454
Well, I suppose not.

00:16:53.514 --> 00:16:55.284
Oh no!

00:16:55.344 --> 00:16:56.486
What?

00:16:56.546 --> 00:16:59.437
I know it's not cheap, but...

00:16:59.457 --> 00:17:00.088
Shhh!

00:17:00.148 --> 00:17:01.768
It's Sarah!

00:17:01.828 --> 00:17:05.140
I say, looking desperately for somewhere to hide.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:06.361
So?

00:17:06.421 --> 00:17:09.803
She thinks that I'm going to the fair with her tonight.

00:17:09.863 --> 00:17:10.903
And?

00:17:10.964 --> 00:17:11.844
Quick!

00:17:11.904 --> 00:17:13.175
Hide behind!

00:17:13.235 --> 00:17:14.375
Oh no!

00:17:14.436 --> 00:17:16.887
It's too late she can see us!

00:17:16.947 --> 00:17:20.699
Tell her that you're going to Grands because she's not very well.

00:17:20.759 --> 00:17:22.653
I can't do that!

00:17:22.714 --> 00:17:25.728
But then Sarah is in the shop.

00:17:25.788 --> 00:17:28.889
I want to go out with then more than anything.

00:17:28.949 --> 00:17:31.850
But I can't lie to my best friend.

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:33.440
Can I?

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:35.101
Hi, Holly.

00:17:35.161 --> 00:17:37.062
I thought it was you.

00:17:37.122 --> 00:17:39.823
She says with a big smile.

00:17:39.883 --> 00:17:41.433
Rosie.

00:17:41.494 --> 00:17:44.555
She says, but without a smile.

00:17:44.615 --> 00:17:47.406
I'm really looking forward to tonight.

00:17:47.466 --> 00:17:51.172
Mum says she'll take us for a pizza first too.

00:17:51.232 --> 00:17:53.827
Actually, I...

00:17:53.888 --> 00:17:57.010
I need to talk to you about tonight.

00:17:57.070 --> 00:17:58.530
I...

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.192
I can't.

00:18:00.252 --> 00:18:02.714
I can't come to the fair, you see.

00:18:02.774 --> 00:18:04.866
I feel terrible.

00:18:04.926 --> 00:18:09.188
But the words are out of my mouth before I can stop them.

00:18:09.248 --> 00:18:10.960
It's my grand.

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:13.212
She's sick and needs me.

00:18:13.272 --> 00:18:15.143
You know how it is.

00:18:15.203 --> 00:18:16.284
Oh.

00:18:16.344 --> 00:18:19.080
Well, I hope she feels better soon.

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:24.348
She looks so disappointed and I feel terrible.

00:18:24.408 --> 00:18:26.180
I've got to go!

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:27.792
See you tomorrow!"

00:18:27.852 --> 00:18:32.496
I say quickly and walk away before she can see my red face.

00:18:32.556 --> 00:18:37.308
When we get back home, it's already late afternoon.

00:18:37.368 --> 00:18:41.652
Rosie puts some music on and does my hair and makeup.

00:18:41.712 --> 00:18:44.244
Then I put on my new clothes.

00:18:44.304 --> 00:18:48.335
I'm excited and I soon forget about Sarah.

00:18:48.395 --> 00:18:49.654
There.

00:18:49.714 --> 00:18:51.094
All finished.

00:18:51.154 --> 00:18:52.905
Says Rosie happily.

00:18:52.965 --> 00:18:54.596
What do you think?

00:18:54.656 --> 00:18:57.506
I don't really like purple eyeshadow.

00:18:57.566 --> 00:19:00.168
And the orange top is very tight.

00:19:00.228 --> 00:19:04.430
Well, she asks waiting for my answer.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:05.946
It's great!

00:19:06.006 --> 00:19:08.434
I say and try to smile.

00:19:08.494 --> 00:19:13.598
But there is so much makeup on my face that I can't smile too much.

00:19:13.658 --> 00:19:15.780
Ben will love it.

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:17.182
Trust me.

00:19:17.242 --> 00:19:19.324
Are you going to the fair too?

00:19:19.384 --> 00:19:22.117
I ask, trying to keep calm.

00:19:22.177 --> 00:19:25.310
In 24 minutes I'm meeting Ben.

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:27.382
No, my foot hurts.

00:19:27.442 --> 00:19:29.805
I'm going home to watch a DVD.

00:19:29.865 --> 00:19:33.946
That's not much fun, I say, as we go out the door.

00:19:34.006 --> 00:19:39.417
Don't worry about me, just have a good time, she says.

00:19:39.477 --> 00:19:43.228
Thanks Rosie, I say as I get on the bus.

00:19:43.288 --> 00:19:46.839
Rosie smiles and waves as I sit down.

00:19:46.899 --> 00:19:51.432
I'm not surprised her foot hurts after shopping all day.

00:19:51.492 --> 00:19:58.069
Rosie continues waving, and then the bus turns the corner.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:03.734
But when the bus disappears, her smile disappears too.

00:20:03.794 --> 00:20:09.210
She takes her mobile phone and calls Julie.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:15.544
Everything is perfect, she says.

00:20:15.605 --> 00:20:26.433
Chapter 4 The Truth When I get off the bus, I'm really excited.

00:20:26.493 --> 00:20:29.446
I even say goodbye to the bus driver.

00:20:29.506 --> 00:20:33.740
But when I get to the fair, Ben isn't there.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:39.024
I sit down on a bench just outside the entrance and look at my watch.

00:20:39.085 --> 00:20:40.025
Again.

00:20:40.045 --> 00:20:42.928
605.

00:20:42.988 --> 00:20:45.169
Is Ben excited like me?

00:20:45.189 --> 00:20:46.960
615.

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:53.514
I watch people go in, families, groups of friends and couples holding hands.

00:20:53.574 --> 00:20:55.906
Will Ben hold my hand?

00:20:55.966 --> 00:21:00.300
615 Maybe his bus is late.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:03.182
Traffic is usually bad at this time of day.

00:21:03.202 --> 00:21:08.306
630 Where are you, Ben?

00:21:08.326 --> 00:21:17.066
633 Maybe his parents are angry with him for some reason, and they won't let him go out.

00:21:17.126 --> 00:21:21.087
And because he hasn't got my mobile number, he can't call me.

00:21:21.107 --> 00:21:28.028
634 Why didn't I give him my mobile number?

00:21:28.048 --> 00:21:33.489
635 Why didn't I ask for his?

00:21:33.509 --> 00:21:42.827
645 Did he say that he's going to meet me outside the fair or inside?

00:21:42.888 --> 00:21:46.079
I was so excited when he phoned.

00:21:46.139 --> 00:21:48.260
I can't remember.

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:51.282
Maybe he's inside thinking that I'm not coming.

00:21:51.302 --> 00:21:55.774
I quickly get up and go through the entrance.

00:21:55.834 --> 00:22:01.336
The loud music and bright lights make everything seem magical as I look for Ben.

00:22:01.396 --> 00:22:02.998
Holy!

00:22:03.058 --> 00:22:06.813
Someone calls my name, but it isn't Ben.

00:22:06.873 --> 00:22:10.690
I thought your gran was sick, Holly.

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:12.670
Sarah!

00:22:12.731 --> 00:22:14.092
I...

00:22:14.152 --> 00:22:17.334
I say and my face goes red.

00:22:17.394 --> 00:22:21.138
You lied to me, she says.

00:22:21.198 --> 00:22:23.499
Her mum and dad look at me.

00:22:23.559 --> 00:22:26.602
They seem more disappointed than angry.

00:22:26.662 --> 00:22:33.166
I suddenly feel very silly in the short skirt and make up that Rosie gave me.

00:22:33.226 --> 00:22:35.422
I can explain.

00:22:35.482 --> 00:22:42.036
I try to touch her arm, but she moves away, her eyes full of angry tears.

00:22:42.096 --> 00:22:44.457
I'm not interested.

00:22:44.517 --> 00:22:46.978
I thought you were my friend.

00:22:47.038 --> 00:22:51.889
My best friend, she says, and then walks away.

00:22:51.909 --> 00:22:57.020
I stand there alone, and I feel stupid.

00:22:57.080 --> 00:23:03.771
First the basketball match, then Ben, and now Sarah isn't my friend anymore.

00:23:03.831 --> 00:23:05.991
What's the matter, Holly?

00:23:06.051 --> 00:23:08.192
Someone says behind me.

00:23:08.252 --> 00:23:10.164
It's Rosie.

00:23:10.224 --> 00:23:11.964
Oh, Rosie.

00:23:12.024 --> 00:23:13.966
I'm so glad to see you.

00:23:14.026 --> 00:23:15.246
Bend it.

00:23:15.306 --> 00:23:19.268
But before I finish, I can hear laughter.

00:23:19.328 --> 00:23:24.968
Horrible, horrible laughter.

00:23:25.028 --> 00:23:30.986
The laughter is coming from Rosie's friends.

00:23:31.046 --> 00:23:38.059
For a moment, I just stand there while they laugh and point at me my silly clothes and my terrible makeup.

00:23:38.119 --> 00:23:41.010
How could I be so stupid?

00:23:41.070 --> 00:23:43.492
I thought she was my friend.

00:23:43.552 --> 00:23:46.732
I thought she was nice and wanted to help me.

00:23:46.792 --> 00:23:51.304
Did you really believe that Ben wants to go out with you?

00:23:51.365 --> 00:23:54.688
She says.

00:23:54.749 --> 00:24:04.554
She starts to laugh again and her friends laugh even louder and louder and louder.

00:24:04.614 --> 00:24:07.085
I turn and start to run.

00:24:07.145 --> 00:24:09.266
This is a nightmare.

00:24:09.326 --> 00:24:11.166
I'll wake up soon.

00:24:11.226 --> 00:24:13.578
I'll wake up soon.

00:24:13.638 --> 00:24:20.770
I tell myself again and again, but I know that I will remember tonight forever.

00:24:20.830 --> 00:24:24.480
When I am alone, I sit down on a bench.

00:24:24.540 --> 00:24:30.159
Then I realized that it is the same bench as before and I start to cry.

00:24:30.179 --> 00:24:33.670
I was so happy then.

00:24:33.730 --> 00:24:38.231
It was only half an hour ago, but it seems more like 10 years.

00:24:38.291 --> 00:24:41.842
How can everything change so quickly?

00:24:41.902 --> 00:24:44.983
Are you okay?

00:24:45.043 --> 00:24:47.504
An old woman asks me.

00:24:47.564 --> 00:24:49.624
I look up quickly.

00:24:49.684 --> 00:24:54.437
She's sitting next to me, a grey cat on her knee.

00:24:54.497 --> 00:25:00.022
I can tell you your future if you want.

00:25:00.082 --> 00:25:02.894
I don't want to know about my future.

00:25:02.954 --> 00:25:05.025
I have no future.

00:25:05.085 --> 00:25:09.678
I stand up and start to walk away, ready to go home.

00:25:09.738 --> 00:25:14.140
But if you can make wishes come true, I think.

00:25:14.200 --> 00:25:17.892
Five pounds.

00:25:17.952 --> 00:25:19.794
Says the old woman.

00:25:19.854 --> 00:25:25.168
Something in her voice makes me stop walking and take my purse out of my bag.

00:25:25.228 --> 00:25:33.395
I can make wishes come true for five pounds.

00:25:33.456 --> 00:25:36.808
I've only got five pounds, I say.

00:25:36.868 --> 00:25:40.720
But when I look up, the old woman is not there anymore.

00:25:40.780 --> 00:25:48.235
I don't know why, but I am happy when I see her standing outside a caravan, the cat in her arms.

00:25:48.295 --> 00:25:52.029
Another three cats move hungrily between her legs.

00:25:52.090 --> 00:25:56.173
How did she get that far so quickly?

00:25:56.233 --> 00:26:01.444
I don't know why I don't just go home, but I walk towards her.

00:26:01.504 --> 00:26:09.086
I give her the money, she opens the door and I go inside the caravan.

00:26:09.146 --> 00:26:15.807
Listening activity 1.

00:26:15.867 --> 00:26:20.072
What time is Holly going to meet Ben?

00:26:20.132 --> 00:26:23.517
Would you like to go to the fair, Holly?

00:26:23.577 --> 00:26:24.638
Yes.

00:26:24.698 --> 00:26:26.228
That would be great.

00:26:26.288 --> 00:26:27.779
What time?

00:26:27.840 --> 00:26:30.000
How about 6 o'clock?

00:26:30.060 --> 00:26:31.652
I'm not sure.

00:26:31.712 --> 00:26:35.124
I've got a doctor's appointment at half past five.

00:26:35.184 --> 00:26:37.865
How about a quarter to seven then?

00:26:37.925 --> 00:26:39.246
Excellent.

00:26:39.306 --> 00:26:41.296
See you then.

00:26:41.356 --> 00:26:43.488
Two.

00:26:43.548 --> 00:26:47.871
What time is Sarah's train leaving today?

00:26:47.931 --> 00:26:50.013
Excuse me.

00:26:50.073 --> 00:26:53.786
Can you tell me what time the train to London is, please?

00:26:53.846 --> 00:26:56.668
Just one moment, please.

00:26:56.728 --> 00:26:59.780
There's one at three ten.

00:26:59.840 --> 00:27:01.802
That's too early.

00:27:01.862 --> 00:27:03.643
Is there a later train?

00:27:03.703 --> 00:27:04.604
Yes.

00:27:04.664 --> 00:27:08.166
The next train to London leaves at three fifty.

00:27:08.226 --> 00:27:10.558
But there's a one hour delay.

00:27:10.618 --> 00:27:11.689
Okay.

00:27:11.749 --> 00:27:12.630
Thank you.

00:27:12.690 --> 00:27:14.441
Bye.

00:27:14.501 --> 00:27:16.572
Three.

00:27:16.632 --> 00:27:20.274
What time does Rosie's party start?

00:27:20.334 --> 00:27:23.948
Are you going to Rosie's party, Julie?

00:27:24.008 --> 00:27:28.352
I'd like to, but I've got to see my grand in the afternoon.

00:27:28.412 --> 00:27:31.174
I won't leave her house until six.

00:27:31.234 --> 00:27:32.605
That's okay.

00:27:32.665 --> 00:27:37.178
It starts at seven thirty, but I'm not going until eight o'clock.

00:27:37.238 --> 00:27:39.090
Do you want to go together?

00:27:39.150 --> 00:27:40.822
That's a good idea.

00:27:40.882 --> 00:27:42.403
I can't wait.

00:27:42.463 --> 00:27:43.704
Me too.

00:27:43.764 --> 00:27:46.538
Bye.

00:27:46.598 --> 00:28:00.106
Traveling Funfares Groups of people called Showmen travel throughout the year to different areas of the country to set up Funfares.

00:28:00.166 --> 00:28:06.330
These are called Traveling Funfares because they do not stay in the same place.

00:28:06.390 --> 00:28:12.636
The type of Funfares that always stays in the same place is called a theme park.

00:28:12.696 --> 00:28:18.432
Fun fairs are very popular all over Britain and in many other places in the world.

00:28:18.492 --> 00:28:23.984
They are especially popular with teenagers and families with young children.

00:28:24.044 --> 00:28:27.774
Each Fun Fair has a lot of different rides.

00:28:27.834 --> 00:28:35.870
There are rides for adults and older children and teenagers, sometimes called thrill rides.

00:28:35.930 --> 00:28:46.900
These rides move very fast, going backwards and forwards, up and down, and often use a lot of spinning or falling.

00:28:46.960 --> 00:28:52.314
They are a lot of fun, but are also very scary.

00:28:52.374 --> 00:28:58.247
There are also lots of rides for younger children, such as train rides.

00:28:58.307 --> 00:29:02.572
These are slower and not scary.

00:29:02.632 --> 00:29:08.658
There are stalls where you can play games, such as throwing games.

00:29:08.718 --> 00:29:12.942
At these stalls, people pay to complete a task.

00:29:13.002 --> 00:29:17.556
For example, hitting some moving objects with a ball.

00:29:17.616 --> 00:29:26.024
If the person is successful, he or she wins a prize, often a giant teddy bear.

00:29:26.084 --> 00:29:36.372
These stalls are very popular with teenage couples because it is considered romantic for a boy to win a prize for his girlfriend.

00:29:36.433 --> 00:29:40.016
There are other stalls where you can buy food.

00:29:40.076 --> 00:29:48.712
Hot dogs, hamburgers and chips are popular, but candy floss is the traditional funfair food.

00:29:48.772 --> 00:29:53.254
Most funfares also have a fortune teller.

00:29:53.314 --> 00:30:01.704
This person, usually a woman, tells a person what will happen to him or her in the future.

00:30:01.764 --> 00:30:07.026
Sometimes these things come true, but sometimes they don't.

00:30:07.086 --> 00:30:10.307
Do you believe in fortune tellers?

00:30:10.367 --> 00:30:12.117
Hoppings.

00:30:12.177 --> 00:30:15.680
Europe's largest travelling fanfare.

00:30:15.740 --> 00:30:24.178
Throughout the year, town Moore, in Newcastle-upon-Tine, is home to about 400 cows.

00:30:24.238 --> 00:30:31.975
But for a week in June, the 30-acre space is covered with over 60 rides and numerous stalls.

00:30:32.035 --> 00:30:39.722
Travelling fares from all parts of the country come together, and the Hoppings happens.

00:30:39.782 --> 00:30:46.854
This funfair began in 1882 and has over a million visitors each year.

00:30:46.914 --> 00:30:51.356
It is now bigger than ever.

00:30:51.416 --> 00:31:05.222
Chapter 5 Make a Wish Are you sure you want things to change, Holly?

00:31:05.282 --> 00:31:07.566
The old woman asks me.

00:31:07.626 --> 00:31:11.351
Yes, I'm totally sure, I say.

00:31:11.411 --> 00:31:17.984
The old woman looks at me for a long time, then she takes a birthday cake out of the fridge.

00:31:18.044 --> 00:31:23.736
It looks delicious, and in the middle there is one pink candle.

00:31:23.796 --> 00:31:28.287
She puts the cake on the table in front of me and lights the candle.

00:31:28.347 --> 00:31:36.264
Then, very quietly, she says, Happy birthday, Holly.

00:31:36.324 --> 00:31:42.039
Blow out the candle and make your wish.

00:31:42.100 --> 00:31:47.852
It all feels very strange, like I'm watching it all on television.

00:31:47.912 --> 00:31:55.474
I close my eyes and blow out the candle, repeating my wish again and again to myself.

00:31:55.534 --> 00:32:01.486
When I open my eyes, for a moment everything is black, there is nothing.

00:32:01.546 --> 00:32:05.120
And then everything starts to become clear again.

00:32:05.180 --> 00:32:13.478
First the lights of the fair shine through the closed curtains, and then there is the ticked talk of the clock on the wall.

00:32:13.538 --> 00:32:16.170
But I am alone in the caravan.

00:32:16.231 --> 00:32:20.104
The old woman and her cats are no longer here.

00:32:20.164 --> 00:32:23.746
I stand up quickly and run outside.

00:32:23.807 --> 00:32:27.837
I want to call out for her, but I don't know her name.

00:32:27.897 --> 00:32:30.086
I don't feel different.

00:32:30.146 --> 00:32:32.376
The wish isn't working.

00:32:32.436 --> 00:32:36.508
How could I believe that the old woman can change my life?

00:32:36.567 --> 00:32:42.940
How could I believe that Rosie wanted to be my friend or that then really wanted to go out with me?

00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:46.040
I must be really stupid.

00:32:46.100 --> 00:32:49.042
And I gave her five pounds.

00:32:49.102 --> 00:32:50.682
Rosie!

00:32:50.702 --> 00:32:53.902
A voice calls from far away.

00:32:53.962 --> 00:32:59.123
But then, how did the old woman know it's my birthday tomorrow?

00:32:59.183 --> 00:33:01.224
Rosie!

00:33:01.284 --> 00:33:03.826
Says the voice closer now.

00:33:03.886 --> 00:33:06.297
And how did she know my name?

00:33:06.357 --> 00:33:07.758
Did I tell her?

00:33:07.818 --> 00:33:09.880
I don't think so.

00:33:09.940 --> 00:33:12.891
Maybe this is all another trick.

00:33:12.951 --> 00:33:16.034
Someone touches my arm and says again.

00:33:16.094 --> 00:33:17.705
Rosie.

00:33:17.765 --> 00:33:19.856
I quickly turn around.

00:33:19.916 --> 00:33:22.628
Julie and Jane are standing in front of me.

00:33:22.688 --> 00:33:24.399
Didn't you hear us?

00:33:24.459 --> 00:33:25.750
Julie says.

00:33:25.810 --> 00:33:27.641
What are you doing here?

00:33:27.701 --> 00:33:29.142
Are you okay?

00:33:29.202 --> 00:33:32.584
You look a little strange.

00:33:32.644 --> 00:33:33.843
I...

00:33:33.903 --> 00:33:37.104
That was a great trick.

00:33:37.164 --> 00:33:40.086
She says and starts to laugh.

00:33:40.146 --> 00:33:43.477
Everyone at school is going to laugh at this.

00:33:43.537 --> 00:33:45.378
That's good!

00:33:45.438 --> 00:33:48.999
Why didn't I take a photo with my mobile phone?

00:33:49.059 --> 00:33:51.599
But I don't hear her anymore.

00:33:51.660 --> 00:33:56.271
Behind Julie there is a mirror and the girl looking back at me.

00:33:56.331 --> 00:34:00.986
Her blonde hair is perfect, long and straight.

00:34:01.047 --> 00:34:03.420
Not like a clown's hair.

00:34:03.481 --> 00:34:06.421
My wish really did come true.

00:34:06.481 --> 00:34:08.251
I'm Rosie.

00:34:08.312 --> 00:34:10.182
I'm Rosie.

00:34:10.242 --> 00:34:14.763
Being Rosie is the best feeling in the world.

00:34:14.823 --> 00:34:18.034
When I was Holly, nobody noticed me.

00:34:18.094 --> 00:34:24.845
But now that I'm Rosie, everybody wants to talk to me, ask what I think and be my friend.

00:34:24.905 --> 00:34:30.396
I smile and laugh, and I don't feel scared of what people think about me.

00:34:30.456 --> 00:34:34.237
I'm Rosie, and I feel like I could run a marathon.

00:34:34.297 --> 00:34:35.987
Climb mine to Everest.

00:34:36.047 --> 00:34:38.137
I could do anything.

00:34:38.198 --> 00:34:40.448
Another voice shouts.

00:34:40.508 --> 00:34:43.109
Rosie, Rosie.

00:34:43.169 --> 00:34:44.689
It's Ben.

00:34:44.749 --> 00:34:48.270
He's running, and he looks very worried.

00:34:48.330 --> 00:34:50.500
But he's still gorgeous.

00:34:50.560 --> 00:34:54.659
I feel more like Holly again as I try to say something.

00:34:54.719 --> 00:34:56.878
Do you know if Holly is here?

00:34:56.939 --> 00:34:58.020
He asks.

00:34:58.080 --> 00:35:01.642
I couldn't find that DVD you said I had, Rosie.

00:35:01.702 --> 00:35:03.904
Are you sure you gave it to me?

00:35:03.964 --> 00:35:07.276
I still don't know why you needed it tonight.

00:35:07.336 --> 00:35:10.329
Oh, I hope Holly is still here.

00:35:10.389 --> 00:35:12.672
He says, looking around.

00:35:12.732 --> 00:35:17.013
Julian, Jane, start to laugh.

00:35:17.073 --> 00:35:19.834
What?

00:35:19.894 --> 00:35:20.924
Says Ben.

00:35:20.984 --> 00:35:22.336
Why are you laughing?

00:35:22.396 --> 00:35:23.846
What's so funny?

00:35:23.906 --> 00:35:28.350
Ben, his eyes become cold, and he looks at me angrily.

00:35:28.410 --> 00:35:31.062
What did you do to her, Rosie?

00:35:31.122 --> 00:35:31.833
Me?

00:35:31.853 --> 00:35:33.854
I...

00:35:33.915 --> 00:35:37.197
It was so funny, Ben.

00:35:37.257 --> 00:35:38.548
Says Julie.

00:35:38.608 --> 00:35:41.570
There was no DVD, Rosie, right?

00:35:41.630 --> 00:35:42.921
He says coldly.

00:35:42.941 --> 00:35:45.182
I...

00:35:45.242 --> 00:35:48.060
Everyone quickly stops laughing.

00:35:48.120 --> 00:35:51.348
They turn to look at me as Ben walks away.

00:35:51.408 --> 00:35:53.660
I start to become Red.

00:35:53.720 --> 00:35:57.954
I want to shout after him that I'm really Holly, not Rosie.

00:35:58.014 --> 00:35:59.976
It wasn't me who did this.

00:36:00.036 --> 00:36:01.717
I didn't do it.

00:36:01.778 --> 00:36:04.159
But who will believe me?

00:36:04.220 --> 00:36:07.162
After that nothing seems the same.

00:36:07.222 --> 00:36:09.484
Everyone starts to go home.

00:36:09.544 --> 00:36:11.456
It's 11 p.m.

00:36:11.516 --> 00:36:13.698
I never go home this late.

00:36:13.758 --> 00:36:16.534
My dad will definitely ground me.

00:36:16.594 --> 00:36:22.550
But as I run towards home, I suddenly realize, I'm Rosie now.

00:36:22.610 --> 00:36:25.201
I have to go to Rosie's house.

00:36:25.262 --> 00:36:28.994
Rosie's new house is the biggest in the village.

00:36:29.054 --> 00:36:33.666
Her friend say it even has a swimming pool and six servants.

00:36:33.726 --> 00:36:38.999
It will be fun to live the life of the rich girl, the girl who has everything.

00:36:39.059 --> 00:36:42.501
But when I get back, the front door is locked.

00:36:42.561 --> 00:36:44.412
The lights are all out.

00:36:44.472 --> 00:36:46.916
It looks like nobody's at home.

00:36:46.976 --> 00:36:51.911
I knock again, loud at this time, but there is still no answer.

00:36:51.971 --> 00:36:54.662
Where are my aunt and uncle?

00:36:54.722 --> 00:36:56.883
I look in Rosie's bag.

00:36:56.943 --> 00:37:01.444
At the bottom, I find a key and I go inside.

00:37:01.504 --> 00:37:06.566
The first thing I notice about the house is that it is huge.

00:37:06.626 --> 00:37:08.836
I start to look around.

00:37:08.897 --> 00:37:14.129
There are a lot of beautiful things, but there are no family photos.

00:37:14.189 --> 00:37:17.702
But there are lots of photos in every room of my house.

00:37:17.762 --> 00:37:20.994
Everything here is perfect and expensive.

00:37:21.054 --> 00:37:25.396
But there is no love and it feels cold.

00:37:25.456 --> 00:37:29.768
I go upstairs but still there are no angry parents.

00:37:29.828 --> 00:37:34.382
My mum and dad are always angry with me when I come back late.

00:37:34.442 --> 00:37:40.960
But now, as I get into Rosie's bed, I would like that more than anything.

00:37:41.020 --> 00:37:44.206
I want them to shout, be angry.

00:37:44.266 --> 00:37:45.476
Anything.

00:37:45.536 --> 00:37:49.348
I just want them here.

00:37:49.408 --> 00:37:53.019
Chapter 6.

00:37:53.079 --> 00:37:56.270
Happy Birthday.

00:37:56.330 --> 00:38:01.412
I can't sleep, so I get up early the next morning.

00:38:01.472 --> 00:38:05.308
I choose some of Rosie's expensive clothes to wear.

00:38:05.368 --> 00:38:12.434
I always liked Rosie's clothes, but when I look in the mirror, there is no smile on my face.

00:38:12.494 --> 00:38:16.605
Today's our birthday Rosie, I say to myself.

00:38:16.665 --> 00:38:21.126
I'm sure that Aunt Lillian Uncle Pete will have a brilliant day planned.

00:38:21.186 --> 00:38:27.078
First there will be lots of presents to open, then we'll go somewhere special together.

00:38:27.138 --> 00:38:33.499
We'll go to an expensive restaurant for lunch, and tonight there will be the best party of my life.

00:38:33.559 --> 00:38:39.203
When I was Holly, I was only going to go bowling with Mum, Dad and Sarah.

00:38:39.264 --> 00:38:42.196
But I don't think Sarah will go now.

00:38:42.256 --> 00:38:44.588
Not after yesterday.

00:38:44.648 --> 00:38:46.590
I'm very sorry.

00:38:46.650 --> 00:38:49.322
Says the cook when I go downstairs.

00:38:49.382 --> 00:38:51.494
She looks very worried.

00:38:51.554 --> 00:38:53.906
Your breakfast isn't ready yet.

00:38:53.966 --> 00:38:55.388
It's just that.

00:38:55.448 --> 00:38:58.350
You don't usually get up this early.

00:38:58.410 --> 00:39:01.469
She says and hurries back into the kitchen.

00:39:01.529 --> 00:39:08.589
When she comes back, she puts my breakfast on the table, says, Happy Birthday Rosie.

00:39:08.649 --> 00:39:10.440
And walks away.

00:39:10.500 --> 00:39:15.141
Excuse me, I ask before she gets to the kitchen.

00:39:15.202 --> 00:39:16.762
Where's Aunt?

00:39:16.822 --> 00:39:19.263
I mean, Mum and Dad.

00:39:19.323 --> 00:39:21.104
Don't you remember?

00:39:21.164 --> 00:39:24.035
They're away on business until Wednesday.

00:39:24.095 --> 00:39:26.986
But they left your presents in the living room.

00:39:27.046 --> 00:39:31.640
I'm not hungry, so I get up and go into the living room.

00:39:31.700 --> 00:39:35.076
On the table, there are lots of presents.

00:39:35.136 --> 00:39:38.868
I open them and there is everything I always wanted.

00:39:38.928 --> 00:39:45.183
There's a new laptop computer, a diamond bracelet and a new mobile phone.

00:39:45.244 --> 00:39:49.637
But there is no one to watch me open them and to say thank you to.

00:39:49.657 --> 00:39:54.010
I can't believe I feel even emptier than before.

00:39:54.070 --> 00:39:56.670
Maybe going shopping will help.

00:39:56.730 --> 00:39:59.589
I phone Julie first and then Jane.

00:39:59.649 --> 00:40:01.910
I ask them if they want to come too.

00:40:01.970 --> 00:40:04.941
But they both have something to do or somewhere to go.

00:40:05.001 --> 00:40:06.962
So I go by myself.

00:40:07.022 --> 00:40:10.442
But it's not the same and I don't buy anything.

00:40:10.502 --> 00:40:13.034
Nothing looks nice anymore.

00:40:13.094 --> 00:40:15.904
There is nothing I want today.

00:40:15.964 --> 00:40:20.256
When Mum and I go shopping we always have a laugh and an ice cream.

00:40:20.316 --> 00:40:23.028
But today nothing has any flavor.

00:40:23.088 --> 00:40:29.990
I walk past the bowling alley, and from a distance I watch as Mum and Dad have fun with Rosie.

00:40:30.050 --> 00:40:33.391
Rosie is now me, Ollie.

00:40:33.451 --> 00:40:38.542
Rosie too is smiling and relaxed, and she looks happier than ever.

00:40:38.602 --> 00:40:40.933
Then I see Ben.

00:40:40.993 --> 00:40:42.483
Ben!

00:40:42.543 --> 00:40:44.344
What are you doing here?

00:40:44.404 --> 00:40:45.814
I smile.

00:40:45.874 --> 00:40:48.015
But he doesn't smile back.

00:40:48.075 --> 00:40:52.474
When he sees me, his eyes become dark and angry.

00:40:52.534 --> 00:40:55.755
You know, I really like Holly.

00:40:55.815 --> 00:41:01.920
I just hope she will understand when I explained that I didn't know about your stupid trick.

00:41:01.980 --> 00:41:07.364
How can you be so horrible to your own cousin, to anyone?

00:41:07.424 --> 00:41:12.458
Then he walks on and I am left alone once more.

00:41:12.518 --> 00:41:15.080
I want to be me again.

00:41:15.140 --> 00:41:17.652
But how can that happen now?

00:41:17.712 --> 00:41:20.054
There's nothing I can do.

00:41:20.114 --> 00:41:22.520
This is my life now.

00:41:22.580 --> 00:41:25.896
Or is it?

00:41:25.956 --> 00:41:29.188
Listening activity.

00:41:29.208 --> 00:41:30.688
1.

00:41:30.748 --> 00:41:33.100
1915.

00:41:33.160 --> 00:41:34.070
2.

00:41:34.130 --> 00:41:34.270
2000.

00:41:34.290 --> 00:41:34.370
3.

00:41:34.390 --> 00:41:34.651
1625.

00:41:34.671 --> 00:41:43.349
4.

00:41:43.409 --> 00:41:52.207
1764.

00:41:52.227 --> 00:41:52.347
5.

00:41:52.407 --> 00:41:52.688
2012.

00:41:52.708 --> 00:41:52.748
6.

00:41:52.768 --> 00:41:53.148
1989.

00:41:53.208 --> 00:41:53.328
7.

00:41:53.388 --> 00:41:57.170
24 February 1997.

00:41:57.191 --> 00:42:07.346
8.

00:42:07.406 --> 00:42:37.596
Tuesday 16th June 2020 Chapter 7 Finding the Old Woman I love spring and today is a perfect day of blue sky and warm sunshine.

00:42:37.656 --> 00:42:41.158
But as I go to the fair I don't notice the weather.

00:42:41.218 --> 00:42:42.986
I am too nervous.

00:42:43.046 --> 00:42:45.244
Will the old woman be there?

00:42:45.304 --> 00:42:47.075
Will she make me holly again?

00:42:47.095 --> 00:42:49.926
I have lots of money now.

00:42:49.986 --> 00:42:53.768
As Rosie, I can give her all the money she asks for.

00:42:53.828 --> 00:42:58.440
I think about being holly again and I smile and walk faster.

00:42:58.500 --> 00:43:05.494
But when I get to the fair there is no loud music, no bright lights, no rides and no people.

00:43:05.554 --> 00:43:08.767
There are only two caravans left.

00:43:08.827 --> 00:43:13.020
As I go towards one, I can see a very tall man.

00:43:13.080 --> 00:43:18.001
He is connecting one of the caravans to a big lorry and is about to leave.

00:43:18.061 --> 00:43:20.812
Excuse me, I ask.

00:43:20.872 --> 00:43:22.592
Where's the fair?

00:43:22.652 --> 00:43:25.703
It's going back to Russia.

00:43:25.763 --> 00:43:28.824
He says in a very loud voice.

00:43:28.884 --> 00:43:31.364
He has a Russian accent.

00:43:31.424 --> 00:43:32.895
Russia?

00:43:32.955 --> 00:43:34.335
But it can't.

00:43:34.395 --> 00:43:38.975
I have to see the old woman, the one that makes wishes come true.

00:43:39.035 --> 00:43:40.900
but the man doesn't answer.

00:43:40.920 --> 00:43:46.962
He gets into the lorry and as he starts the engine.

00:43:47.022 --> 00:43:52.739
I say, please, you don't understand.

00:43:52.799 --> 00:43:55.400
I'm not really the person you can see.

00:43:55.460 --> 00:43:57.950
My wish changed me into my cousin.

00:43:58.010 --> 00:44:00.171
But now I want to be me again.

00:44:00.231 --> 00:44:03.292
Please, I can't be like this forever.

00:44:03.312 --> 00:44:08.373
My eyes fill with tears and I can't help crying.

00:44:08.433 --> 00:44:11.564
Only then does he turn to look at me.

00:44:11.624 --> 00:44:14.264
For a moment he doesn't say anything.

00:44:14.324 --> 00:44:16.606
Please, I say.

00:44:16.666 --> 00:44:21.872
The fair stops once more before we go back to Russia.

00:44:21.932 --> 00:44:29.150
But in London, if you want to see the old woman, you'll have to go to London.

00:44:29.210 --> 00:44:30.562
Tonight.

00:44:30.622 --> 00:44:33.414
Tomorrow morning, we all leave.

00:44:33.474 --> 00:44:35.976
Then he drives away.

00:44:36.036 --> 00:44:37.725
London.

00:44:37.785 --> 00:44:40.304
I need to get a train now.

00:44:40.364 --> 00:44:43.646
Mum and Dad will be so angry with me.

00:44:43.706 --> 00:44:49.532
They don't want me to go on trains on my own until I'm 16 in two years.

00:44:49.592 --> 00:44:52.754
But I must go now.

00:44:52.814 --> 00:44:54.666
I run back home.

00:44:54.726 --> 00:44:58.248
When I get back, the house is full of people.

00:44:58.308 --> 00:45:00.561
It's my birthday party.

00:45:00.621 --> 00:45:02.954
Everyone is there early.

00:45:03.014 --> 00:45:07.806
But nobody notices when I go in or when I go back out with a bag.

00:45:07.866 --> 00:45:11.038
They're all dancing, eating and laughing.

00:45:11.098 --> 00:45:13.839
But I have to get to London.

00:45:13.899 --> 00:45:20.382
My dad thinks I'm still a baby and my mum always says that my bedroom is always untidy.

00:45:20.442 --> 00:45:22.939
But I miss them so much.

00:45:22.999 --> 00:45:26.016
It will take a couple of hours to get to London.

00:45:26.076 --> 00:45:29.928
The train is quite empty and there are lots of places to sit.

00:45:29.988 --> 00:45:36.912
But because it's my first time on a train by myself, I sit next to a young mother and her crying baby.

00:45:36.972 --> 00:45:39.393
This makes me feel safer.

00:45:39.453 --> 00:45:46.877
As I put my bag down, the mother smiles and says, Sorry about Poppy, it's her teeth.

00:45:46.937 --> 00:45:49.120
She's only six months old.

00:45:49.180 --> 00:45:56.518
That's okay, I try to smile, but when I see the mother and her baby, my eyes feel with tears.

00:45:56.578 --> 00:46:00.871
Excuse me, can you look after my bag for a moment?

00:46:00.931 --> 00:46:04.424
I ask, and I get up and go to the toilet.

00:46:04.484 --> 00:46:07.176
I wash my face with cold water.

00:46:07.236 --> 00:46:11.158
But when I go back to my seat, my eyes are still red.

00:46:11.218 --> 00:46:15.302
I see the mother and her baby getting off the train as I get back.

00:46:15.362 --> 00:46:18.664
She waves and smiles at me from the platform.

00:46:18.724 --> 00:46:22.164
I sit alone until the train gets to London.

00:46:22.224 --> 00:46:34.647
When I finally get off the train, my arms and legs feel heavy and tired, so I sit down in a cafe to have a coffee and something to eat and think about what to do next.

00:46:34.707 --> 00:46:37.277
I eat my sandwich quickly.

00:46:37.338 --> 00:46:40.428
I must find the fair and the old woman.

00:46:40.488 --> 00:46:48.796
I ask the waitress for the bill and I look for my money, but my purse is not in my bag.

00:46:48.856 --> 00:46:53.164
Listening activity.

00:46:53.224 --> 00:46:59.020
Good morning and welcome to Weatherwise 7 Day Forecast.

00:46:59.080 --> 00:47:06.709
For those of you hoping for a sunny start to the week, I'm afraid we are expecting heavy rain for Monday.

00:47:06.769 --> 00:47:13.376
The weather will get worse and storms are forecast for both Tuesday and Wednesday.

00:47:13.437 --> 00:47:17.389
But on Thursday you can leave your umbrella at home.

00:47:17.449 --> 00:47:21.580
It will be sunny with temperatures of 25 in the south.

00:47:21.640 --> 00:47:27.694
Friday will be cloudy though, and on Saturday there will be strong winds.

00:47:27.754 --> 00:47:34.737
But then the sun will return for another hot and sunny Sunday.

00:47:34.797 --> 00:47:41.984
Chapter 8 I want to be me.

00:47:42.044 --> 00:47:45.478
Please tell me this isn't happening.

00:47:45.538 --> 00:47:47.509
My purse was here before.

00:47:47.569 --> 00:47:50.270
I know I had it when I got on the train.

00:47:50.330 --> 00:47:52.091
Where is it now?

00:47:52.151 --> 00:47:54.722
I empty my bag onto the table.

00:47:54.782 --> 00:47:58.284
There are my keys, some eyeshadow and a lipstick.

00:47:58.344 --> 00:48:01.306
But my purse and mobile phone aren't there.

00:48:01.366 --> 00:48:03.856
How can I pay the bill now?

00:48:03.917 --> 00:48:08.549
I've only got the small bag with the change from when I bought my train ticket.

00:48:08.609 --> 00:48:11.840
I can't even phone anybody to come and help.

00:48:11.900 --> 00:48:20.176
I watch the waitress as she takes another order before disappearing inside the cafe and I know I have to do something wrong.

00:48:20.236 --> 00:48:23.698
I look around and check that no one is watching me.

00:48:23.758 --> 00:48:25.820
Then I get up and run.

00:48:25.840 --> 00:48:28.692
I run as fast as I can.

00:48:28.752 --> 00:48:36.388
And when I think I can't run anymore, I think about the police arresting me and I run even faster.

00:48:36.448 --> 00:48:40.566
I only stop when I am sure I am about to die.

00:48:40.626 --> 00:48:48.725
It is now dark and I am in London, one of the busiest cities in the world, with no money.

00:48:48.785 --> 00:48:51.376
Where am I going to sleep tonight?

00:48:51.436 --> 00:49:02.199
The maid won't be worried because I told her that I was going to stay with Julie for a few days and my aunt and uncle are too busy with business meetings and making even more money to worry.

00:49:02.259 --> 00:49:05.528
But then I see a poster.

00:49:05.588 --> 00:49:07.588
One night only.

00:49:07.649 --> 00:49:11.662
The world famous Stavisloski Family Fair.

00:49:11.722 --> 00:49:13.444
Covent Garden.

00:49:13.504 --> 00:49:16.498
Last stop on European tour.

00:49:16.558 --> 00:49:18.460
Don't miss it.

00:49:18.520 --> 00:49:26.432
I ran as fast as I can to the tube station and with the last of my money I buy a ticket to Covent Garden.

00:49:26.492 --> 00:49:29.568
I have to change trains twice to get there.

00:49:29.628 --> 00:49:33.450
There is a train in a few minutes, so I quickly run to the platform.

00:49:33.510 --> 00:49:37.431
But after fifteen minutes, the train is still not there.

00:49:37.491 --> 00:49:41.312
The train arriving at platform two is delayed.

00:49:41.372 --> 00:49:43.583
We apologise.

00:49:43.644 --> 00:49:49.566
I wait and wait and then the train finally arrives.

00:49:49.626 --> 00:49:52.486
When I get to the fair, it is late.

00:49:52.546 --> 00:49:56.194
There are only a few people left and they are leaving.

00:49:56.254 --> 00:50:00.872
I see three girls who look about my age working on one of the rides.

00:50:00.932 --> 00:50:03.313
Excuse me, I say.

00:50:03.373 --> 00:50:05.714
I'm looking for an elderly lady.

00:50:05.774 --> 00:50:06.915
I continue.

00:50:06.975 --> 00:50:11.838
And when I finish telling them my story, I ask, is she here?

00:50:11.898 --> 00:50:14.919
Yes, says one of the girls.

00:50:14.979 --> 00:50:20.967
She has short dark hair and very big blue eyes that are very difficult not to look at.

00:50:21.027 --> 00:50:22.592
She's here.

00:50:22.652 --> 00:50:23.944
Excellent.

00:50:24.004 --> 00:50:25.424
I smile.

00:50:25.484 --> 00:50:27.856
Everything is going to be okay.

00:50:27.916 --> 00:50:34.899
But you must know that she is the 8th daughter of the world famous magician, Slavistavislovski.

00:50:34.959 --> 00:50:38.881
8th daughters have very special powers.

00:50:38.941 --> 00:50:42.774
But once they are used, they cannot go back.

00:50:42.834 --> 00:50:43.946
But...

00:50:44.006 --> 00:50:45.619
You don't understand.

00:50:45.639 --> 00:50:48.040
I can't be like this forever.

00:50:48.060 --> 00:50:58.034
If I can just see her, I'm sure that if I explain everything, we'll take you to her, but she'll tell you the same thing.

00:50:58.094 --> 00:51:01.796
Nervously, I follow them to a caravan.

00:51:01.856 --> 00:51:07.590
They go inside, and after the longest five minutes of my life, they come out again.

00:51:07.650 --> 00:51:11.632
You can go in now, says the girl with the blue eyes.

00:51:11.692 --> 00:51:17.234
I climb the two steps, and when I see her there, I am sure she will help.

00:51:17.294 --> 00:51:21.446
I'm so pleased to see you, I say smiling.

00:51:21.506 --> 00:51:25.058
But she holds her hand up to stop me.

00:51:25.118 --> 00:51:29.618
Lord Mila told me why you're here.

00:51:29.678 --> 00:51:33.116
I'm sorry, but I can do nothing.

00:51:33.176 --> 00:51:40.138
But I asked you if you were sure you wanted things to change.

00:51:40.198 --> 00:51:42.658
You said yes.

00:51:42.718 --> 00:51:43.819
I know.

00:51:43.839 --> 00:51:45.759
I was wrong.

00:51:45.819 --> 00:51:47.170
Please.

00:51:47.230 --> 00:51:50.000
You have to turn me back into Holly.

00:51:50.060 --> 00:51:52.928
I don't have any more money, but...

00:51:52.988 --> 00:52:01.120
I know, the young mother on the train took your money and your phone, too.

00:52:01.180 --> 00:52:03.140
How do you know that?

00:52:03.200 --> 00:52:09.144
I am the eighth daughter of the famous Slavistavislovski.

00:52:09.204 --> 00:52:20.824
When I was ten, my father said to me, Octavia, you have a special gift.

00:52:20.884 --> 00:52:25.248
But you must use that gift carefully.

00:52:25.308 --> 00:52:33.132
Everyone has one wish, and only one wish.

00:52:33.192 --> 00:52:35.784
You had one wish.

00:52:35.844 --> 00:52:38.915
You wanted to be rosy.

00:52:38.975 --> 00:52:42.486
I made your wish come true.

00:52:42.546 --> 00:52:49.858
I'm sorry, but I cannot help.

00:52:49.918 --> 00:53:00.424
Chapter 9 No More Wishes But you have to do something.

00:53:00.484 --> 00:53:03.706
I can't be Rosie for one more minute.

00:53:03.766 --> 00:53:05.547
I want to be Holly.

00:53:05.607 --> 00:53:07.298
I want my family back.

00:53:07.358 --> 00:53:08.590
Please.

00:53:08.650 --> 00:53:12.542
When I get back, I can get you some more money.

00:53:12.602 --> 00:53:16.095
I'm not rich like Rosie, but I do have some money.

00:53:16.155 --> 00:53:17.606
Please.

00:53:17.666 --> 00:53:21.725
I can't give you another wish.

00:53:21.785 --> 00:53:25.704
But you will be Holly again.

00:53:25.764 --> 00:53:29.476
My wishes aren't forever.

00:53:29.536 --> 00:53:34.139
You will be Holly again at midnight.

00:53:34.199 --> 00:53:38.682
She puts a hand on my shoulder and smiles.

00:53:38.743 --> 00:53:50.775
I thank her and I'm about to leave when she says, In the future, be careful what you wish for.

00:53:50.835 --> 00:54:00.288
As the train leaves the station, I look out of the window at all the lights in people's houses, bright against the black sky.

00:54:00.348 --> 00:54:07.714
I see Rosie's face looking at me, and for the first time since I became her, I am happy.

00:54:07.774 --> 00:54:16.080
I try to keep my eyes open, but I'm very tired, and as I sit back in my seat, my eyes start to close.

00:54:16.140 --> 00:54:18.166
I fight sleep.

00:54:18.226 --> 00:54:21.110
I must stay awake, I must.

00:54:21.170 --> 00:54:24.142
But eventually sleep wins.

00:54:24.203 --> 00:54:32.548
I dream of my bedroom, the posters on the wall, the mess and mum shouting that I must tidy up in the morning.

00:54:32.609 --> 00:54:43.490
I dream of my favourite things like watching DVDs on rainy Sunday afternoons, chocolate ice cream and getting into a clean bed after having a long relaxing bath.

00:54:43.551 --> 00:54:47.158
Holly, breakfast's ready!

00:54:47.218 --> 00:54:51.342
Someone shouts, and at first I think I'm still sleeping.

00:54:51.402 --> 00:54:53.264
But then I hear it again.

00:54:53.324 --> 00:54:55.026
It sounds like mum.

00:54:55.086 --> 00:54:56.638
My mum.

00:54:56.698 --> 00:55:00.132
I open my eyes, but I'm not on the train.

00:55:00.192 --> 00:55:01.344
I'm home.

00:55:01.404 --> 00:55:02.900
In my bed.

00:55:02.960 --> 00:55:10.024
I throw the duvet off and run down the stairs, but when I pass the mirror in the hall I stop suddenly.

00:55:10.084 --> 00:55:16.950
I have to see, but opening my eyes to check that I'm not Rosie anymore is very hard.

00:55:17.010 --> 00:55:20.194
Please let me look like a clown.

00:55:20.254 --> 00:55:23.045
Slowly I open my eyes.

00:55:23.106 --> 00:55:24.438
Yes!

00:55:24.498 --> 00:55:28.440
I shout so loud that mum comes out of the kitchen.

00:55:28.500 --> 00:55:30.730
Holly, what's the matter?

00:55:30.790 --> 00:55:32.311
Nothing, Mum.

00:55:32.371 --> 00:55:34.592
Everything's perfect.

00:55:34.652 --> 00:55:36.874
I say giving her a big kiss.

00:55:36.934 --> 00:55:37.955
Good.

00:55:38.015 --> 00:55:41.417
Now come and get your breakfast before it goes cold.

00:55:41.477 --> 00:55:44.929
Mum is surprised and laughs.

00:55:44.989 --> 00:55:48.162
There is a knock on the front door.

00:55:48.222 --> 00:55:51.043
Please, can you open the door, Holly?

00:55:51.103 --> 00:55:54.716
Shouts, Mum, before going back into the kitchen.

00:55:54.776 --> 00:55:58.514
Is it the postman or the milkman coming for his money?

00:55:58.574 --> 00:56:02.672
But it's Rosie, and she looks very sad.

00:56:02.732 --> 00:56:05.154
For a moment we just look at each other.

00:56:05.174 --> 00:56:07.736
Do you want to go for a walk?

00:56:07.796 --> 00:56:11.238
She says, I think we need to talk.

00:56:11.298 --> 00:56:20.284
We walk for a while and then I say, I'm not looking forward to going to school tomorrow, not after the basketball match.

00:56:20.344 --> 00:56:22.716
And I must speak to Sarah.

00:56:22.776 --> 00:56:26.427
Don't worry Holly, Sarah will understand.

00:56:26.487 --> 00:56:31.648
And as for everyone else, no one will say anything to you.

00:56:31.708 --> 00:56:34.040
Rosie says with a smile.

00:56:34.100 --> 00:56:38.532
I'll make sure that no one is horrible to you ever again.

00:56:38.592 --> 00:56:41.914
I'm so sorry for what I did to you.

00:56:41.975 --> 00:56:45.497
You know, Ben really likes you.

00:56:45.557 --> 00:56:47.718
You should go and see him.

00:56:47.778 --> 00:56:49.799
That's okay Rosie.

00:56:49.860 --> 00:56:54.352
Let's forget about it and be friends as well as cousins.

00:56:54.412 --> 00:56:57.990
I say smiling at my cousin.

00:56:58.050 --> 00:57:09.198
As Holly and Rosie walk out of the front door, Holly's mum starts going upstairs.

00:57:09.258 --> 00:57:12.679
She sees something on the floor.

00:57:12.739 --> 00:57:15.850
She picks it up.

00:57:15.910 --> 00:57:18.800
A train ticket to London?

00:57:18.860 --> 00:57:21.301
Where did that come from?

00:57:21.361 --> 00:57:29.411
She puts it in her pocket and continues with her day.

00:57:29.472 --> 00:57:34.724
The only person I know who goes to London is my sister Lily.

00:57:34.784 --> 00:57:41.720
She says to herself later as she is cleaning the bathroom.

00:57:41.780 --> 00:57:49.105
I wish I were rich like Lily so that I could go shopping all day and not have to do housework.

00:57:49.166 --> 00:57:54.552
Just for one day I'd like to be Lily.

00:57:54.612 --> 00:58:02.842
She says, and then suddenly, something strange happens.

